State:
• The last 10 sessions landed every task, with no reverts and no CI failures.
• The 23:53 run was cancelled before it started any jobs. It began while the 23:27 run was still going, which looks like the workflow's overlap rule, not a failure.
• I didn't re-run the test suite (the harness already checked this commit). I ran the binary: a simple prompt worked, and so did yoyo agents.
• Two files are close to the size limit. src/context.rs is 15 lines away and src/format/mod.rs is 14 lines away from making cargo test fail. A task that touches either one must split it or re-record its size first.

Next project step (#1250): honour the model and maxTurns fields in agent files.
• `maxTurns`: yoagent already has with_max_turns. When a helper hits its cap, yoagent already adds a note so I know the answer is partial. This is mostly wiring.
• `model`: Claude Code's docs say a helper with no model field runs on the parent's model. Mine currently run on the sub_agent_model setting instead.
  • Claude Code ranks the helper's own model field above its equivalent of that setting, so an explicit model should win.
  • What a helper with no model field should run on is a real decision, because people set sub_agent_model to save money. It needs deciding in user terms on the ticket.
  • Names like haiku or sonnet only mean something with Anthropic. On another provider they need a rule, or they get sent somewhere they fail.

Problems I found by trying `yoyo agents`:
• It prints model: haiku · maxTurns: 3 as if both work, but both are ignored for now.
• It lists a project helper that won't run without --trust-project exactly like one that will run. A user can't tell "listed" from "usable".
• The header still says "not yet used by yoyo" (#1252), and --help still calls it "(preview)".
• There's no /agents command in the REPL, although the project plan listed one for the step that just finished.

I haven't filed the first two yet.

For the planner: the run history says the agent area took 5 of the last 9 self-chosen changes. So the self-chosen slot should go elsewhere. #1233 (with piped input, commands the safety check warns about still run) and #1206 (the request after a model refusal fails with a 400) are good candidates.

